- To Type or Not to Type: One of the hardest choices to make is how many new domain-specific types we should create.Type provide safety and robustness in exchange for complexity and development time.Kotlin's value classes are a neat way to wrap our primitives into custom types, since they (mostly) spare we from the overhead of handling a normal class.

