### Terminologies

- Anemic objects antipattern

- Endofunctor: Functors that map a category on themselves.

- Generics: Are type builders

- Category: A mathematical concept introduced to define the relation between things
  in the most abstract way possible.
  
- Functors: error-aware magic arrows (maps two categories together) - 

  - Give us control over when the query is executed.
  - We only want to run the query when it's correct, and at a minimum (ensure that the
    projections are up-to-date)
  - There may be additional checks that need to be performed => allow us to separate
    the technical infrastructure concerns from the business requirements in a clean
    and original manner.
  - As a result conveys the message that there is a change of context when running a
    query.
  - Using a functor for our ProjectionQuery is Laziness.
  
- Aggregate: A set of related entities that can be changed together inside an atomic
  transaction.
  
- Entity states

- Entity: is defined based on its identity, and a set of related entities that can be
  changed together is called an aggregate.
  
- State-transitions/ transition-sourcing/ transitional entities

- Commands (messages that arrive from outside, can fail)

- Events (the record that the state of the system has changed, can't fail)

- A monoid without a neutral element => a semigroup.

- Union types (sum, coproduct)/ data class (product types)/ function types (exponential types)
- Accumulator/ Reducer/ Recursion.

- immutable - "snapshot in time" of any list.

- Low Cardinality

- Christmas tree indentation -> resolve by let function.

- Testing cycle

- Modulith - a modular monolith (Implementing the Clean Architecture (Sebastian Buczynski)

- module:
  (is a cohesive package of code with its own vocabulary (in particular having a
  specific name for a user). It groups related functionalities and exposes them using a
  module API. A well-designed module resembles a microservice, though there is no
  network communication needed to use the module).
  
- Hub: Use an interface to wrap all the domain logic and keep it separated from the external adapter (Port & Adapter - Hexagonal Architecture). The hub defines and abstracts upon the boundaries between the domain and the technical layer - in a very precise and oddly satisfying way.
  The domain stays inside the hub and only communicates with the rest of the app using specific funtions.

